+// ================================================================================================ (training part 5) IRED: the sums in the backward
+// transition_bwd_reduce ran after the whole backward (a programmatic dependent: its blocks start as the backward's CTAs leave, ~2.4-3.5 us
+// of tail). Here the R replicas of a hidden slice meet on a counter as soon as their partials are stored and each sums 1 / R of the slice
+// (the DW role ends before the DX role); the first 16 DW CTAs then wait for every DX CTA and sum dgamma | dbeta, 16 columns each. The
+// orders are transition_bwd_reduce's (replicas in replica order from 0; dgamma | dbeta rows g, g + 16, ... per lane group, then the 16
+// group sums in group order): the same bits. All CTAs are resident (one per SM, the host launches SM-count CTAs).
+// Counters (zeroed once per device, back to 0 at the end of every launch): cnt[s] slice s (R arrivals), cnt[8] DX CTAs (ndx), cnt[9] exits
+// (G). The last CTA to exit (every other CTA is past its waits) resets cnt[0..9]; the next launch reads them after griddepcontrol.wait.
+// (A monotonic launch-number form hung: launches with other R / ndx share the buffer.)
+DEVI unsigned ld_acq(const unsigned* p) { unsigned v; asm volatile("ld.acquire.gpu.global.u32 %0, [%1];" : "=r"(v) : "l"(p) : "memory"); return v; }
+DEVI void arrive_rel(unsigned* p) { asm volatile("red.release.gpu.global.add.u32 [%0], 1;" :: "l"(p) : "memory"); }
